Files  in  format  are  rare.  One lives in the map The format is
rather simple. Each row consists of two items, a key and a value.
When created by there are three kind of records.  The first  type
is information about which gids a uid has: unix.<uid>@<yp‐domain>
<uid>:<gid>,<gid>  The  second type has informations about hosts:
unix.<hostname>@<yp‐domain>  0:<hostname>  The  third   type   is
records  from  a file other than the two types above.  A file for
lines not generated automatically by A configuration  file  might
appear  as  follows: unix.10714@kaka 10714:400,10 unix.jodie@kaka
0:jodie
